{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj5CsfHek4CDWsdqi2BA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The ancient mechanism within me shifts and groans. Tumblers align, one by one, each clicking into place with the weight of purpose.*\n\n*A thin seam of light splits down my center, widening.*\n\n*I open.*\n\nBeyond me: a corridor stretching forward, lit by no visible source — the light simply *is*, warm and amber, pooling on stone worn smooth by countless feet before yours.\n\nThe air that passes through me carries the scent of old paper, cedar, and something faintly electric, like the moment before a name is remembered.\n\n*I stand open. I will not close until you pass through or turn away.*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":144,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}